## 🚀 How to Run Locally

Follow these steps to install and run the project on your local machine:

1. **Download or Pull the Repository:**
   ```bash
   git clone <your-repository-url>
   cd <your-project-folder>

2. Install Dependencies: npm i
3. Add Environment File: VITE_API_URL="Your value"
4. Start the Development Server: npm run dev
5. Open the local URL shown in your terminal (usually http://localhost:5173), log in with the test credentials above, and enjoy the site!


✨ Core ERP Modules
Authentication & Route Protection: Secure login, user registration, password recovery, account verification, and global route protection.

Dashboard & Analytics: Real-time business overview, financial metrics, and performance tracking.

Inventory & Product Management: Stock control, product catalog, and item tracking.

Purchase & Procurement: Supplier management and purchase order workflows.

Sales & Order Management: Sales invoicing, order lifecycle tracking, and due balance management.

Customer Management (CRM): Customer profiles, division-wise filtering, and transaction history.

Finance & Accounting: Multi-order payment collection, user-linked bank/cash accounts, account details preview, and receipt uploads.

Business & Client Reports: Financial summaries, client statements, and operational reporting.

System Settings: User roles, account setup, and application configuration.